## Services

- [AI Strategy & Advisory](https://cognis.group/our-services/ai-strategy-advisory/): Choose the right AI opportunities and get a clear plan with priorities, owners, costs, safeguards and measures of success.
- [AI Training & Workforce Development](https://cognis.group/our-services/ai-training-workforce-development/): Practical training that helps leaders and teams work better, check AI output and use approved tools safely.
- [AI Agent & Automation Engineering](https://cognis.group/our-services/ai-agent-automation-engineering/): AI tools that handle agreed steps in business processes, with clear limits, human approval and monitoring.

## Insights

- [Securing AI Agents in Production: A 2026 Threat Model](https://cognis.group/blog/securing-ai-agents-in-production/): Kola Olatunde’s boundary-first control model for identity, tools, memory, approvals, logging, and incident response.
- [Enterprise RAG Security](https://cognis.group/blog/enterprise-rag-security-prompt-injection-data-exfiltration/): Kola Olatunde on prompt injection, data exfiltration, retrieval-time access control, and secure ingestion.
- [AI Governance in Africa in 2026](https://cognis.group/blog/ai-governance-africa-2026/): Kola Olatunde’s operating-control framework for multi-jurisdiction African enterprises.
- [From Copilot to Coworker](https://cognis.group/blog/from-copilot-to-coworker-productizing-ai-agents/): Tosin Salami’s product framework for bounded jobs, trust, staged autonomy, and agent launch criteria.
- [The AI Agent Product Operating System](https://cognis.group/blog/ai-agent-product-operating-system/): Tosin Salami on evals, production telemetry, unit economics, versioning, and lifecycle governance.
- [Why Most Enterprise AI Strategies Fail Before They Start](https://cognis.group/blog/why-most-enterprise-ai-strategies-fail-before-they-start/): Common failure modes in enterprise AI adoption.
- [Building AI Agents That Actually Ship](https://cognis.group/blog/building-ai-agents-that-actually-ship/): From proof of concept to production-grade agent deployment.
- [AI Governance Is Not Optional](https://cognis.group/blog/ai-governance-is-not-optional/): Building governance before deployment, not after.
- [The Real ROI of AI](https://cognis.group/blog/the-real-roi-of-ai/): How to measure AI impact beyond efficiency metrics.
- [Making Your Workforce AI-Ready](https://cognis.group/blog/making-your-workforce-ai-ready/): Developing AI literacy from boardroom to operations.
- [AI-Native Operations for African Enterprises](https://cognis.group/blog/ai-native-operations-for-african-enterprises/): How African enterprises can leapfrog into AI-native operations.

## About

Cognis Group Limited is registered with the Corporate Affairs Commission (Lagos, Nigeria). Co-founded in 2024 by Supreme Oyewumi and Kola Olatunde. Offices in Cheyenne, Wyoming (USA), Ontario (Canada), and Oniru, Victoria Island, Lagos (Nigeria). Serves organisations across Africa, Europe, and the Americas.

Motto: Quod Tango Muto ("What we touch, we change.")

Contact: info@cognis.group | +2349080001101

